--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -170,3 +170,13 @@ python scripts/export_preview.py
 
 After launch, submit `/sitemap.xml` in Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools, inspect each language URL, and verify that production allows crawling while staging does not. These account actions remain owner-run.
 
+
+## Elementor Pro connection and private statistics (0.2.0)
+
+`/font-to-elementor-pro/` connects WordPress through an administrator redirect and one-time session state. Opaque credentials stay in browser tab session storage and are sent only to WordPress. The plugin requires HTTPS and active Elementor Pro, and registers installed fonts in the FontReady font group rather than the native Custom Fonts manager. The plugin source and ZIP are in `wordpress/`. Deploy both releases together.
+
+Run `python manage.py migrate` before starting web and worker processes. Create an owner account with `python manage.py createsuperuser` using a private password, then sign in at `/owner/`. Only superusers can view the dashboard; it is noindex and contains no external analytics. No default owner credentials exist. Successful conversions are deduplicated in durable tables, surviving file expiry. Daily totals use Africa/Lagos time, and top font families can be compared over 7, 30 and 365 days. Connections and installs are explicitly browser-reported, not independently audited server receipts. Statistics start with this release; no historical data is fabricated.
+
+The migration adds `ConversionMetric`, `SiteConnection` and `PublishMetric`. Only dates, family names, counts, formats, domain names and internal deduplication IDs are retained. `/privacy/` explains retention and connection consent. To fulfill a domain deletion request, delete its SiteConnection row (related PublishMetric rows cascade). Historical aggregate conversion statistics are independent of domains.
+
+Before release, run live WordPress/Elementor Pro tests and WordPress Plugin Check as documented in the plugin repository. This code has not been submitted to WordPress.org.
