@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+{% load static %}<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>FontReady · Privacy and service details</title><link rel="canonical" href="https://fontready.com/privacy/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="{% static 'app.css' %}"></head><body><main class="shell" style="max-width:760px;padding:50px 20px"><a class="brand" href="/">FontReady<span>.</span></a><h1>Privacy & service details</h1><p>FontReady converts uploaded fonts on its servers. Download kits expire after 24 minutes. Original uploads are removed after conversion; expired outputs are cleaned up by the background maintenance service.</p><h2>Conversion statistics</h2><p>We retain conversion dates, font family names, variant counts and output format names to understand usage. These aggregate records survive file deletion. They contain no font files, visitor IP addresses, or browser session identifiers.</p><h2>Connecting WordPress</h2><p>Installing and activating the plugin enables font installation on your website. Connection requires your WordPress administrator account, HTTPS and Elementor Pro. At connection, you confirm your domain and agree to share the domain, installed font totals and successful installation reports with FontReady. The plugin performs no automatic tracking on activation.</p><p>Authentication credentials stay in your browser tab's session storage and your WordPress site stores their hash. FontReady's server never receives the credential. Connections expire after seven days and can be revoked in WordPress → FontReady. Font files are sent directly from your browser to your WordPress site; nothing is sent to Elementor's servers.</p><p>Browser-reported connection and installation statistics include the website domain and activity dates. Disconnecting does not erase historical counts. For a domain record deletion request, contact the site operator through <a href="https://ademolaalabi.com/">Ademola Alabi's website</a>.</p><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>The public website uses Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to understand website usage. The connection form is masked for Clarity. Private owner pages load neither service. Connection fragments are removed before analytics scripts load.</p><h2>Your installed fonts</h2><p>Installed fonts are served locally from WordPress uploads/fontready. Families appear in Elementor's FontReady group; the plugin does not create entries in Elementor Pro's native Custom Fonts manager. Deactivation stops loading the fonts but keeps their files for reactivation. Fonts must be licensed for use on your website.</p><p>FontReady is an independent tool and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Elementor.</p></main></body></html>
